module wyd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }
import frcrimp.deadlines.{ SentencingScheduled }

// The District of Wyoming's own criminal periods, counted under the
// criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). No trigger
// carries a service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added days follow the
// manner of service, which is not modeled here.
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP or Speedy Trial Act periods stay in lit/frcrimp
// and are only named here: the Probation Office discloses the presentence
// report no later than 35 days before the sentencing hearing, unless the
// defendant waives the minimum period, and the report is deemed disclosed
// when filed in CM/ECF (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 32.1(d); FRCrimP 32(e)(2));
// objections are filed in CM/ECF within 14 days after its filing (D. Wyo.
// L.Cr.R. 32.1(d); FRCrimP 32(f)(1)); the probation officer submits the
// report and addendum to the judge not later than 7 days before the
// hearing (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 32.1(g); FRCrimP 32(g)); a party appeals a
// magistrate judge's judgment by a notice of appeal within 14 days after
// its entry (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 58.1; FRCrimP 58(g)(2)(B)); and at arraignment
// counsel and the Court strive for consensus on the status of the 70- and
// 90-day speedy trial periods (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 10; 18 U.S.C. §§ 3161,
// 3164).
//
// Other conditions stay in notes: the sentencing hearing is set no less
// than 70 days after the verdict or change of plea unless the Court orders
// otherwise (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 32.1(a)), a floor on the setting; counsel's
// unavailability for the presentence interview for more than five business
// days after notice is "undue delay" (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 32.1(c)); and,
// absent prior approval, sentencing memoranda and related materials are
// filed not less than three business days before the sentencing hearing
// (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 32.1(l)). Business days are not lowered by the engine.
//
// The earlier D. Wyo. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// are FRCrimP, Speedy Trial Act or constitutional authority and belong to
// lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A victim is served with notice of a subpoena that expressly seeks the
/// victim's personal or confidential information (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R.
/// 17.1(d)).
event VictimSubpoenaNoticeServed()
/// The date set for trial (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 30.1).
event TrialScheduled()
/// The presentence report is disclosed by filing in CM/ECF (D. Wyo.
/// L.Cr.R. 32.1(d), (e)).
event PsrFiled()
/// The case terminates in this Court (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 44.1(e)).
event CaseTerminated()
/// A motion is filed (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 47.1(a)).
event MotionFiled()
/// The Clerk notifies the admitting party that its exhibits are ready for
/// retrieval (D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 55.1(b)).
event ExhibitRetrievalNoticed()

/// D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 17.1(d): a victim may file a sealed motion to quash or
/// modify, or otherwise object to, the subpoena within 14 days after
/// service of the notice; if none is filed, the movant files a sealed ex
/// parte certificate of compliance.
deadline victim-subpoena-objection: 14.days after VictimSubpoenaNoticeServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 17.1(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 30.1: unless otherwise ordered, the parties file
/// proposed voir dire, jury instructions and verdict forms seven calendar
/// days before trial.
deadline voir-dire-instructions-verdict-forms: 7.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 30.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 32.1(b): under 18 U.S.C. § 3664(d)(1), the attorney for
/// the government gives the probation officer a listing of the amounts
/// subject to restitution not later than 60 days before the date initially
/// set for sentencing.
deadline restitution-listing: 60.days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 32.1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 32.1(e): if counsel believe the material in the
/// presentence report is accurate, they file a statement to that effect in
/// CM/ECF within 14 days after its disclosure.
deadline psr-accuracy-statement: 14.days after PsrFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 32.1(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 44.1(e)(1): CJA Form 20 is submitted to the Clerk's
/// office for payment no later than 45 days from the termination of the
/// case in this Court.
deadline cja-form-20: 45.days after CaseTerminated() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 44.1(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 47.1(a): unless otherwise ordered, a party opposing a
/// motion files a response within 14 calendar days after the filing of the
/// motion.
deadline response-period: 14.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 47.1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 55.1(b): exhibits are kept until the time to appeal has
/// expired or any appeal has concluded; if counsel has not retrieved them
/// fourteen days after the Clerk's notice, the Clerk's office destroys
/// them.
deadline exhibit-retrieval: 14.days after ExhibitRetrievalNoticed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Wyo. L.Cr.R. 55.1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
